course: dictionary
lesson: 5856
title: Mama around the world
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «Mama» is a child's word for mother, and it is one of the first words many babies say, because «ma-ma» is an easy sound to make. You will find it in stories, songs and nursery rhymes, such as «Mama bear» and «Mama's gonna buy you a mockingbird».
explain: Other people say it differently. In everyday British English, you are more likely to hear «mum» or «mummy», and in American English «mom» or «mommy». Many families from different backgrounds and languages still use «mama», so it is common across the world.
explain: The same sound can mean the same thing in many languages. «"Ma" and "pa" are among the easiest sounds for babies, so many languages use them for parents (English "mama", Ukrainian "мама", Mandarin "māma", French "maman")». Ukrainian «мама» is the everyday word for mum.
fact: «Mama» is a word for mother, often used by young children.
fact: «Mama» is one of the first words many babies say, because «ma-ma» is easy to say.
fact: «Mama» is informal, so you would use it with family, not in a formal letter.
fact: «Big mama» means a large or powerful woman.
fact: «Mama mia» comes from Italian «mamma mia», meaning «my mother!», and it is an exclamation of surprise.
exercise: The text says «mama» is one of the easiest sounds for babies. Why do so many languages use it for parents? | Only English has it | It is the longest word for mum | *Babies can say «ma-ma» easily | Mothers asked for it in a meeting
exercise: In Ukrainian, «мама» (mama) is the everyday word for what? | Teacher | Dad | *Mum | Friend
exercise: In the rhyme «Mama's gonna buy you a mockingbird», what does Mama mean? | *Mother | A shop | A lullaby | A bird
test: The phrase «mama mia» comes from which language, and what does it mean? | *Italian, meaning «my mother!» | German, meaning «thank you» | French, meaning «good night» | Spanish, meaning «hello»
test: The text says «MAmo!» is what you shout to call Mum. What is it? | A nursery rhyme | *The calling form of «MAma» | The name of a town | A kind of bear
exam: In the phrase «big mama», what does «mama» most likely mean? | *A large or powerful woman | A kind of song | A type of bread | A small baby
